        "offering_role": "product",
        "confidence": 0.96,
        "statement": "As we have progressed with the design work by the Owner’s Engineer and pre-construction services by the CMAR, the estimated cost to construct all required facilities to complete the Mojave Groundwater Bank, including conversion of the Northern Pipeline to water conveyance and construction of the Southern Pipeline, the wellfield and power facilities have increased from our previous estimate of approximately $800 million to our current estimate of between $1.25 and $1.5 billion.",
